      "pins": [
        "C1.1",
        "C1.2"
      ],
      "nets": [
        "GND",
        "Display_Power_Switch"
      ],
      "observed": "C1 is listed as 0.1uF/16V and is connected between GND and the Display_Power_Switch net.",
      "expected": "The specification states that C1 should be a 1uF/25V EPD driver capacitor, matching the PDI default value for this part of the circuit.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"C1\") (value \"0.1uF/16V\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "C2 default: 1 µF/25 V | C1/C5/C7/C8/C9/C10 = 1 µF/25 V | Matches default"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"C1\") (pin \"2\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The EPD power-switch/VDD rail has roughly ten times less bulk capacitance than intended, which can increase ripple and may affect boost-converter stability or EPD power integrity.",
      "confidence": 0.72
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The netlist otherwise closely matches the specification, but C1 on the EPD power rail is 0.1uF/16V where the spec explicitly calls for 1uF/25V, making this the most credible anomaly."
}

